   "guide": "Cefazolin is the surgical-prophylaxis standard; cefuroxime treats respiratory disease; cefotetan and cefoxitin are anaerobe-active cephamycins. Ceftriaxone has broad third-generation indications, while ceftazidime is the best antipseudomonal cephalosporin and later generations cover resistant pathogens."
